   "page": 1,
   "text": "The package holds two N-channel MOSFETs whose drains are one node, reached at pins 2 and 5. Each transistor has its own gate and source and its own body diode from source to drain."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Threshold is 0.45 V to 1.0 V at 250 µA with gate and drain joined. On-resistance is guaranteed at 4.0 V (30 mΩ max, 4.3 A) and 2.5 V (46 mΩ max, 3.4 A). The output curves show 1.8 V on the gate levelling the current near 10 A at 1 V drain-source. Gate charge to 4.5 V is 6.2 nC typical, with the Miller plateau near 1.76 V between about 1.4 and 3.6 nC at 10 V and 3 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "On-resistance rises with temperature: on the normalized scale it is about 0.66 at -50 °C, 1.0 near 25 °C and about 1.61 at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Dissipation is rated 1.25 W at 25 °C ambient, and junction-to-ambient thermal resistance at steady state is 100 °C/W, both mounted on FR4 for t ≤ 10 s. The transient thermal curve is drawn for RθJA = 125 °C/W. Junction and storage temperature span -55 °C to +150 °C."
  },
